# TG-04 stage B: new packages on a kept volume (make tg-upgrade), without making the volume
# again, so tgd's own files (its api id and hash, TDLib's session) stay. Run on a copy of
# the volume, which replaces it only when every step passed. On the console, which holds
# the volume's root: fetch writes the new tg (its program and description) and tgd's new
# description over /packages from the host (one guestfwd rule to a server of those three
# files only, @PORT@; the network is restrict=on); tgd's program is the one already there.
# install replaces each (tg with --keep, its one saved word). @TGHASH@ and @TGDHASH@ are each
# package's identity as install prints it, computed on the host from the files that should
# be installed: a cut transfer or another tgd program on the volume fails here. Then each
# page lists exactly its saved grants, and grants shows no current directory (cwd none).
# tgd is installed again with its whole line (@GRANT@, tgd --install-line, as tg-install
# does), not with --keep, which puts the kept words back in the reverse order: so its page
# is the same, row for row, after every upgrade. tg has one word, kept.
! panicked
! first process ended
! refused
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
> fetch --output /packages/tg/tg http://10.0.2.50:@PORT@/tg\r
limit 120 < \r\n~>
> fetch --output /packages/tg/tg.cmd http://10.0.2.50:@PORT@/tg.cmd\r
limit 60 < \r\n~>
> fetch --output /packages/tgd/tgd.cmd http://10.0.2.50:@PORT@/tgd.cmd\r
limit 60 < \r\n~>
> install --keep /packages/tg\r
limit 120 < tg (sha256 @TGHASH@): 2 files
< replaces tg (sha256 
< kept the saved grants: 
< tg installed with:
<   /data/home/tgd/window.sock  connect to
< \r\n~>
> @GRANT@\r
limit 300 < tgd (sha256 @TGDHASH@): 2 files
< replaces tgd (sha256 
< dropped the saved grants of the old package: 
< tgd installed with:
<   ~/.config/tgd  its own files
<   net: openrouter.ai:443  reach
< \r\n~>
> programs tgd\r
< tgd is an installed program, /apps/tgd/tgd (sha256 @TGDHASH@)
< saved grants:
^ \r\n  +own ~/.config/tgd  ~/.config/tgd  its own files (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 91.108.56.0/22:443  net: 91.108.56.0/22:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 91.108.4.0/22:443  net: 91.108.4.0/22:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 91.108.8.0/22:443  net: 91.108.8.0/22:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 91.108.16.0/22:443  net: 91.108.16.0/22:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 91.108.12.0/22:443  net: 91.108.12.0/22:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 149.154.160.0/20:443  net: 149.154.160.0/20:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 91.105.192.0/23:443  net: 91.105.192.0/23:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 91.108.20.0/22:443  net: 91.108.20.0/22:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net 185.76.151.0/24:443  net: 185.76.151.0/24:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\n  +net openrouter.ai:443  net: openrouter.ai:443  reach (saved)
^ \r\nrunning: none
< \r\n~>
> programs tg\r
< tg is an installed program, /apps/tg/tg (sha256 @TGHASH@)
< saved grants:
^ \r\n  +sock /data/home/tgd/window.sock  /data/home/tgd/window.sock  connect to (saved)
^ \r\nrunning: none
< \r\n~>
> grants tg\r
< tg gets:
< \r\n~>
x current directory
> grants tgd --window\r
< tgd gets (a POSIX program):
< \r\n~>
x current directory
x power off
> poweroff\r
